---
/**
 * /engagement — Read · Implement · Contribute · Reach canonical implementation pathway.
 *
 * Reads as protocol-home guidance, NOT a sales surface. Mentions valuefirstteam.com
 * as the canonical implementing firm without making it the punchline.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageContainer from '../components/PageContainer.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Engagement Pathway"
  description="Four ways to engage with the Value Creation Protocol: read it, implement it, contribute to it, or reach the canonical implementing firm."
  path="/engagement"
  ogImage="og-default.jpg"
>
  <PageContainer wide>
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Engagement"
      title="Read · Implement · Contribute · Reach"
      lede="The protocol is open. Anyone can read, implement, and contribute. The canonical implementing firm exists for organizations that want guided implementation."
    />

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-8">

      <!-- READ -->
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-vcp-teal text-sm">01</span>
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 m-0">Read</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-stone-700 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed">
          Start with the positioning paper. Then the encoding stack. The methodology
          canon is the deep reference — twelve pages covering the frameworks VCP
          encodes. Cold readers should be able to navigate the protocol home in
          a session.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-none p-0 m-0 text-sm">
          <li><a href="/positioning" class="text-stone-700 underline">VCP Positioning Paper</a> — where VCP sits in the protocol stack</li>
          <li><a href="/encoding-stack" class="text-stone-700 underline">Encoding Stack overview</a> — how VCP becomes machine-executable</li>
          <li><a href="/methodology" class="text-stone-700 underline">Methodology canon</a> — twelve framework pages</li>
          <li><a href="/manifestos" class="text-stone-700 underline">Manifestos</a> — long-form treatments</li>
          <li><a href="/glossary" class="text-stone-700 underline">Glossary</a> — full vocabulary</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- IMPLEMENT -->
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-vcp-teal text-sm">02</span>
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 m-0">Implement</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-stone-700 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed">
          Apply VCP in your own organization. The protocol is platform-agnostic;
          the canonical implementing substrate (HubSpot CVP) is one path among
          several. Configuration-over-customization is the operating principle.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-none p-0 m-0 text-sm">
          <li><a href="/hubspot-cvp" class="text-stone-700 underline">HubSpot as CVP</a> — canonical implementing substrate</li>
          <li><a href="/three-orgs" class="text-stone-700 underline">Three-Org Model</a> — where each concern maps</li>
          <li><a href="/unified-views" class="text-stone-700 underline">Four Unified Views</a> — visibility framework</li>
          <li><a href="/ai-native-shift" class="text-stone-700 underline">AI-Native Shift</a> — the transformation pattern</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-5 mb-0 italic">
          No license, no permission required. The protocol is open.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- CONTRIBUTE -->
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-vcp-teal text-sm">03</span>
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 m-0">Contribute</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-stone-700 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed">
          The encoding stack is in active development. Lexicon entries, VCP-Lang
          refinements, Value Graph extensions, and methodology canon corrections
          are welcome. Open the protocol to scrutiny; contribute under the
          editorial governance of the originating firm.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-none p-0 m-0 text-sm">
          <li>Propose <a href="/lexicon" class="text-stone-700 underline">Lexicon</a> entries — new load-bearing terms with industrial counterparts and signals</li>
          <li>Refine <a href="/vcp-lang" class="text-stone-700 underline">VCP-Lang</a> — declarative grammar improvements</li>
          <li>Extend <a href="/value-graph" class="text-stone-700 underline">Value Graph</a> — relational coverage</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-5 mb-0">
          Reach out via the canonical implementing firm (see Reach, below)
          while a formal contribution process is being formed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- REACH -->
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 bg-stone-900 text-stone-100 p-6 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-vcp-teal text-sm">04</span>
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-white m-0">Reach the implementer</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-stone-300 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed">
          VCP was originated and is canonically implemented by
          <a href={SITE.implementer.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-white underline">
            Value-First Team
          </a>.
          For organizations that want guided implementation — pattern recognition,
          architecture review, methodology coaching, or production substrate
          configuration — the team is the canonical place to begin.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-300 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed text-sm">
          The protocol does not require the firm. The firm exists because
          protocols benefit from a reference implementation — and because
          the gap between reading a protocol and operating an organization
          on top of it is bigger than most teams realize on their first
          read.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 mb-0">
          <a
            href={SITE.implementer.url}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md bg-white text-stone-900 text-sm font-medium no-underline hover:bg-stone-100"
          >
            valuefirstteam.com →
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-stone-200">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 m-0 mb-4">Open protocol, opinionated implementation</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        The protocol is open. The implementation is opinionated. Both statements
        are load-bearing. Anyone can implement VCP — the methodology is
        documented, the encoding stack is published, the principles are stated
        with the contrastive precision protocols require. The canonical
        implementer holds opinions about how to do that well, formed over years
        of practice across many organizations. Those opinions are available
        through the canonical implementing firm; they are not preconditions
        for using the protocol.
      </p>
    </section>
  </PageContainer>
</BaseLayout>
